-- =========================================================================
-- kyc_doc_number_drop  —  NOT A LIVE MIGRATION
--
-- The `.PENDING` suffix keeps this out of the Supabase CLI's migration set.
-- It will not run. Renaming it to `<new-timestamp>_kyc_doc_number_drop.sql`
-- is a deliberate, one-way act that must not happen until BOTH gates below
-- are cleared and recorded in docs/dpdpa/README.md.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- GATE 1 — LEGAL (blocking)
--
-- Counsel must confirm Swapngo is not required to retain the full DRIVING
-- LICENCE number for:
--   - Motor Vehicles Act / state transport rules on rental operators
--   - insurance claims and subrogation
--   - police or court requests relating to an incident
--
-- If the answer to any of these is "yes, retain", DO NOT RUN THIS. The
-- correct design in that case is field-level encryption at rest (AES-256-GCM
-- in the backend, key in the environment, decrypt only on an explicitly
-- capability-gated reveal path), not truncation. That is a different change
-- and this file should be deleted rather than adapted.
--
-- Aadhaar is a separate question and a much easier one: nothing in the
-- product reads it, and holding full Aadhaar numbers is the single largest
-- concentration of risk in the schema.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- GATE 2 — SOAK (blocking)
--
-- 20260814100700_kyc_doc_number_prep.sql and the backend change that stops
-- writing full numbers must have been live in production for at least two
-- weeks with no doc-number-related defects. Until this file runs, that work
-- is reversible; afterwards it is not.
--
-- Verify before running:
--   select count(*) from public.user_documents where doc_number_last4 is null;
--   -- expect 0 for every row that has a doc_number
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- AFTER RUNNING — two manual steps this file CANNOT perform
--
-- 1. VACUUM FULL public.user_documents;
--
--    `drop column` only marks the attribute dropped. The bytes survive in
--    dead tuples until the table is rewritten. VACUUM FULL takes an ACCESS
--    EXCLUSIVE lock and cannot run inside a transaction, so it cannot live in
--    a migration file. Schedule it in a maintenance window immediately after.
--
-- 2. Wait out the backup-retention window.
--
--    Supabase PITR backups contain the full numbers for the whole retention
--    period. Until the last backup predating this migration has expired,
--    Swapngo still holds Aadhaar numbers, and NOBODY MAY STATE OTHERWISE —
--    not in the privacy notice, not to a rider, not to the Board. Record the
--    exact date after which the claim becomes true in docs/dpdpa/README.md.
-- =========================================================================

alter table public.user_documents drop column doc_number;
